<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is boundedly invertible on <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation B.11 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) gives the polar decomposition</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the size of the microscopic component created by
reflection, while the isometry <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> records its direction in
<math id="A2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next proposition says that the half-turn acts nearly as <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I</annotation></semantics></math> on the
corresponding microscopic directions <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>